.TH IBND_DISCOVER_FABRIC 3  "July 25, 2008" "OpenIB" "OpenIB Programmer's Manual"
.SH "NAME"
ibnd_discover_fabric, ibnd_destroy_fabric \- initialize ibnetdiscover library.
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.nf
.B #include <infiniband/ibnetdisc.h>
.sp
.BI "ibnd_fabric_t *ibnd_discover_fabric(char " "*ca_name" ", int " "ca_port" ", ib_portid_t " "*from" ", struct ibnd_config " "*config)"
.BI "void ibnd_destroy_fabric(ibnd_fabric_t " "*fabric)"
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.B ibnd_discover_fabric()
Discover the fabric connected to the port specified by ca_name and ca_port.  The "from" parameter is optional and allows one to scan part of a fabric by specifying a node "from", giving the user a "sub-fabric" which is "centered" anywhere they chose.  The "config" parameter tunes the scan (see "struct ibnd_config" below).

ca_name and ca_port may be NULL/0, in which case a default CA and port are used.

.TP
.B struct ibnd_config
Configuration which tunes the scan.  The following members are
recognized (a value of 0 selects the library default):
.RS
.TP
.B show_progress
Indicate that the library should print debug output which shows
its progress through the fabric.
.TP
.B max_smps
Set the number of SMP's which will be issued on the wire simultaneously.
.TP
.B max_hops
Limit the maximum number of hops scanned away from the "from" node.
.TP
.B timeout_ms
Timeout in milliseconds used for each SMP request.
.TP
.B retries
Number of retries for each SMP request.
.TP
.B mkey
MKey used for SMP requests requiring authorization.
.RE

.B ibnd_destroy_fabric()
free all memory and resources associated with the fabric.

.SH "RETURN VALUE"
.B ibnd_discover_fabric()
return NULL on failure, otherwise a valid ibnd_fabric_t object.

.B ibnd_destroy_fabric()
NONE

.SH "EXAMPLES"

.B Discover the entire fabric connected to device "mthca0", port 1.

	struct ibnd_config cfg = { 0 };
	ibnd_fabric_t *fabric = ibnd_discover_fabric("mthca0", 1, NULL, &cfg);
	...
	ibnd_destroy_fabric(fabric);

.B Discover only a single node and those nodes connected to it.

	struct ibnd_config cfg = { .max_hops = 1 };
	ib_portid_t port_id = { 0 };
	...
	str2drpath(&(port_id.drpath), from, 0, 0);
	...
	ibnd_discover_fabric("mthca0", 1, &port_id, &cfg);
	...
.SH "SEE ALSO"
	libibmad, str2drpath
